Code it follows (not included)
------------------------------
The pack runs the model on ComfyUI's own stable-audio classes. Its sampler reproduces what the official tools do at inference:
mimetic-a0 (https://github.com/micknoise/mimetic-a0, commit 9f91b67, MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Mick Grierson) on
stable-audio-tools (https://github.com/Stability-AI/stable-audio-tools, commit 3241adb, MIT, Copyright (c) 2023 Stability AI):
the length with 6 s of headroom, the starting noise, the log-SNR-spaced rectified-flow schedule, and classifier-free guidance
with adaptive projected guidance. No file of either project is copied into this repository.

Models (not included)
---------------------
No model weights are included or downloaded by the nodes. tools/download_model.py fetches, when you run it:
- micknoisemachine/mimetic-a0 (MIT): model_config.json, model.safetensors and/or model.fp16.safetensors, LICENSE, NOTICE,
  README.md, PROMPTING.md. According to its NOTICE and model card, the autoencoder is the ACE-Step 1.5 VAE (MIT), and the
  training data were Freesound clips released as CC0 and synthetic music from the author's procedural generators, partly
  rendered with the GeneralUser GS SoundFont (S. Christian Collins), whose author notes that the origin of some of its samples is
  uncertain.
- google-t5/t5-base (Apache License 2.0): model.safetensors, saved as text_encoders/t5_base.safetensors.
